--- combinators -- function combinator utilities for the handl runtime.
---
--- Single source of truth for the `combinators` stdlib interface: 22
--- function combinators covering composition, control flow, collection
--- iteration, and function manipulation. The Rust bridge in
--- `plugin-lib-stdlib` loads this file via `include_str!`, parses the
--- `cap` declarations for the plugin capability surface, and registers
--- the Rust handls (handlers) in an `OpRegistry` that dispatches each
--- `op` to its native Rust impl. The `fn` module name resolves to this
--- module as an alias (`kit-canonical`'s `StdlibResolver`).
---
--- All 22 functions are FFI atoms (they manipulate `serde_json::Value`
--- callables via `apply_fn` from `crate::shared` and cannot be expressed
--- as pure handl arrows without losing the exact `TypeMismatch` error
--- messages the tests rely on). The `op`/`handl` declaration form
--- (ADR-0077 Phase 2) declares the interface; the Rust `Function` impls
--- in `ops/combinators.rs` provide the logic.
---
--- ## Capability declarations (ADR-0077 Phase 4)
--- combinators.pipe -- pipe a value through a sequence of functions left-to-right.
--- combinators.flow -- compose functions left-to-right into a single inlined function.
--- combinators.compose -- compose functions right-to-left into a single inlined function.
--- combinators.fanout -- apply a value to each of several functions, collecting results into a list.
--- combinators.fanout_fn -- lazy fanout: return a function that splits its input across branches.
--- combinators.choice -- conditional branching: apply one of two functions based on a predicate.
--- combinators.apply -- apply a function to an array of arguments.
--- combinators.flat_map -- map a function over a list and flatten the results.
--- combinators.find -- find the first element of a list satisfying a predicate.
--- combinators.some -- test whether any element of a list satisfies a predicate.
--- combinators.every -- test whether all elements of a list satisfy a predicate.
--- combinators.group_by -- group elements of a list by a key function.
--- combinators.partition -- split a list into matching and non-matching elements.
--- combinators.count_by -- count elements of a list grouped by a key function.
--- combinators.tap -- call a function for its side effect, returning the original value.
--- combinators.match -- pattern-match a value against a sequence of pattern/handler branches.
--- combinators.constantly -- return a function that always yields a fixed value.
--- combinators.flip -- swap the first two parameters of a function.
--- combinators.partial -- partially apply a function by binding its leading arguments.
--- combinators.when -- apply a transform when a predicate holds, otherwise return the value unchanged.
--- combinators.unless -- apply a transform unless a predicate holds, otherwise return the value unchanged.
--- combinators.converge -- apply branches to a value, then combine the results with a combiner.
cap "combinators.pipe"
cap "combinators.flow"
cap "combinators.compose"
cap "combinators.fanout"
cap "combinators.fanout_fn"
cap "combinators.choice"
cap "combinators.apply"
cap "combinators.flat_map"
cap "combinators.find"
cap "combinators.some"
cap "combinators.every"
cap "combinators.group_by"
cap "combinators.partition"
cap "combinators.count_by"
cap "combinators.tap"
cap "combinators.match"
cap "combinators.constantly"
cap "combinators.flip"
cap "combinators.partial"
cap "combinators.when"
cap "combinators.unless"
cap "combinators.converge"
